    "items": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do you know when mountain goats give birth?",
          "Have you watched the deer in labor?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you count the months they are pregnant",
          "so you can know the time they give birth?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They crouch down to give birth to their young;",
          "they deliver their newborn."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Their offspring are healthy and grow up in the open field.",
          "They leave and do not return."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who set the wild donkey free?",
          "Who released the swift donkey from its harness?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I made the desert its home,",
          "and the salty wasteland its dwelling."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It scoffs at the noise of the village",
          "and never hears the shouts of a driver."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It roams the mountains for its pastureland,",
          "searching for anything green."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Would the wild ox be willing to serve you?",
          "Would it spend the night by your feeding trough?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you hold the wild ox to a furrow by its harness?",
          "Will it plow the valleys behind you?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you depend on it because its strength is great?",
          "Would you leave it to do your hard work?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you trust the wild ox to harvest your grain",
          "and bring it to your threshing floor?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The wings of the ostrich flap joyfully,",
          "but are her feathers and plumage like the stork’s? ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "She abandons her eggs on the ground",
          "and lets them be warmed in the sand."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "She forgets that a foot may crush them",
          "or that some wild animal may trample them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "She treats her young harshly, as if they were not her own,",
          "with no fear that her labor may have been in vain."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For God has deprived her of wisdom;",
          "he has not endowed her with understanding."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "When she proudly spreads her wings,",
          "she laughs at the horse and its rider."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do you give strength to the horse?",
          "Do you adorn his neck with a mane?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do you make him leap like a locust?",
          "His proud snorting fills one with terror."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He paws in the valley and rejoices in his strength;",
          "he charges into battle."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He laughs at fear, since he is afraid of nothing;",
          "he does not run from the sword."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A quiver rattles at his side,",
          "along with a flashing spear and a javelin."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He charges ahead with trembling rage;",
          "he cannot stand still at the sound of the ram’s horn."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "When the ram’s horn blasts, he snorts defiantly.",
          "He smells the battle from a distance;",
          "he hears the officers’ shouts and the battle cry."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Does the hawk take flight by your understanding",
          "and spread its wings to the south?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Does the eagle soar at your command",
          "and make its nest on high?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It lives on a cliff where it spends the night;",
          "its stronghold is on a rocky crag."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "From there it searches for prey;",
          "its eyes penetrate the distance."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Its brood gulps down blood,",
          "and where the slain are, it is there."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
